WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.820
The first glimpses we got of Frozen 2 didn't
tell us much, but this latest trailer finally

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.420
gives us a clearer picture of the sequel's
storyline, and we've scoured each and every

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.200
frame for possible clues about what to expect
in Frozen 2.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.160
At the beginning of Frozen, we see the picturesque
kingdom of Arendelle, which sits at the edge

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.380
of the sea, nestled into a wall of towering
cliffs.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.280
Set apart from the village is Arendelle Castle,
rimmed with stone walls and topped with pointed

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.340
green roofs.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.820
However, by the end of the film, the castle
has been transformed, not by the premature

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:37.239
winter which Elsa brings about after losing
control of her powers, but by gleaming ice

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.980
crystals that beautifully adorn all the rooftops
and spires, making the castle appear frosty

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.980
white.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:48.600
The opening shot of the Frozen 2 trailer establishes
that Arendelle Castle is still sporting its

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.050
new look, with the white-tipped castle sitting
next to a peaceful town surrounded by lush

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.260
green grass.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.780
By showing us that Elsa is still glazing the
castle in beautiful layers of ice, we can

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.329
assume that not only is Elsa still reigning
as Queen, but that she's in full control of

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.820
her powers, and at peace with her people.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.640
The Frozen 2 trailer opens with a flashback,
as King Agnarr tells a young Anna and Elsa

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.100
a story about an enchanted forest.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.920
In the story, we see an image of a young golden-haired
boy in Arendelle colors arriving in the forest

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.660
between what appears to be two palace guards.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.860
Then we see a young girl twirling through
the air, and it's hard not to see the similarity

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:29.340
between her and the dark-haired Iduna.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.880
These two children were also shown in an earlier
trailer, where the boy was the one being tossed

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.940
and the girl was the one watching.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:42.100
Is it possible that this is a glimpse of the
first meeting of Agnarr and Iduna, and that

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.720
Iduna is, in fact, from the enchanted forest?

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.820
That could explain where Elsa's magic came
from.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.740
"Born with the powers or cursed?"

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.100
"Born, and they're getting stronger."

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:59.200
Both previous Frozen 2 teasers have shown
us a scene in which one of the sisters was

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.640
surrounded by hovering, icy diamonds.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.920
Now we have another piece of the puzzle, with
the revelation that the diamonds that Elsa

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:11.390
creates seem to match the symbols on the Stonehenge-like
pillars that mark the entrance to the enchanted

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.280
forest.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.500
The trailer makes it appear as though one
of the central questions of Frozen 2 will

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:21.840
be where Elsa's powers came from, and her
ability to create symbols she's presumably

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.460
never seen before may be a major clue.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:29.280
All signs seem to point to some sort of significant
link between Elsa and the enchanted forest,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.340
but we'll have to wait to find out whether
it's the source of her power, the homeland

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:37.120
of one of her parents, or connected to her
magic in some other way.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:44.959
We never had much doubt that Anna, Elsa, Kristoff,
and Olaf would return for Frozen 2, but less

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.100
certain were the fates of all the endearing
side characters from the first film.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:53.720
While it would have been easy enough for Disney
to sweep Frozen's minor characters aside to

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.709
make room for a new crop, we now know at least
a few familiar faces will be making an appearance

00:02:58.709 --> 00:02:59.880
in Frozen 2.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.299
In a shot that presumably takes place shortly
after the citizens of Arendelle have been

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:09.849
forced to flee the village, we see the trolls
Bulda, Cliff, and Pabbie, who cared for Kristoff

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:13.120
as a child, standing in front of the displaced
townspeople.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.200
Behind them is Oaken, the good-natured owner
of Oaken's Trading Post and Sauna, who made

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.560
the most of his brief appearance in the first
film.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.580
"Now back up while I deal with this crook
here."

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.420
"What did you call me?"

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.019
While it seems as though the trolls may still
have a significant role to play in Frozen

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.900
2, chances are that Oaken's appearance will
be more of a cameo.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.320
Still, it's be nice to see him again, and
maybe this time we'll even get to meet his

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.320
family.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.960
"Yoo-hoo, hi family!

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.320
"Yoo-hoo!"

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:51.740
When Elsa hears a mysterious voice calling
to her, she sets out on a quest to figure

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.220
out who it is.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:57.940
Or at least, that's the impression of Frozen
2's plot that we get from the trailer, which

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:02.669
sees Anna immediately volunteering to accompany
her sister as she ventures north in search

00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:03.680
of answers.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:08.959
From the looks of it, Frozen 2 will be largely
Elsa's movie, similar to how Frozen was mostly

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:09.920
about Anna.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.540
Elsa appears to be on her own for a number
of scenes in the trailer, including the one

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.340
where she approaches the wall of mist surrounding
the enchanted forest.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.640
It's easy to miss, since in the very next
shot, Anna is by her side.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:27.780
Elsa's fear of hurting others and her inclination
to isolate herself to her own detriment were

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:33.650
major themes of the first film, so it'll be
interesting to see if, in Frozen 2, Elsa's

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:39.699
tendency to push forward on her own is still
a fatal flaw, or if it has somehow evolved

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.700
into a strength.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.500
At one point in the trailer, Pabbie tells
Elsa that if she wants answers, she has to

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.750
find the source of the voice.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:53.840
As he tells her this, he uses his magic to
give her a vision showing three scenes.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:59.440
The first is a brief glimpse at a bridge that
looks like one of the structures of Arendelle.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:03.220
The next is of two groups of people coming
face to face.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:08.160
Then there's a third image, a staff and a
sword striking together.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.840
This vision could easily foreshadow events
that will occur later in the film, but it

00:05:12.849 --> 00:05:17.440
could also hint at the past event Agnarr referred
to in his story that led to the enchanted

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.180
forest being sealed off.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:23.960
Perhaps the reason it's so important for Elsa
to learn about her past is so that she can

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.600
prevent similar events from happening again
in the future.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:34.440
When Elsa, Anna, Kristoff, and Olaf take off
in their carriage for their trek north, a

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.040
tall, pillar-shaped mountain can be seen in
the distance.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:42.030
If you look closely, you can see Elsa's ice
castle is still there on the side, exactly

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:46.480
as it was when she constructed it during the
"Let It Go" sequence from Frozen.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:51.500
Since Frozen 2 is said to take place three
years after the first film, it's probably

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:56.020
safe to assume that this means Elsa still
spends some time in her ice castle.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:00.479
Although Elsa seems to have made a healthy
home life for herself in Arendelle, it would

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:05.080
make sense if, from time to time, she retreats
to her own northern fortress of solitude to

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:09.900
decompress, burn off some magic, and perhaps
do a bit of general maintenance and upkeep.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:15.180
Once Elsa manages to take her party through
the mist surrounding the enchanted forest,

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:19.409
the Arendelle crew encounters a number of
new characters who have been living on the

00:06:19.409 --> 00:06:20.160
inside.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.800
These include Yelana, who leads the Northuldra
people.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.060
It appears as though they'll have a significant
role to play in Frozen 2.

00:06:28.069 --> 00:06:33.360
We also meet Lieutenant Matthias, who seems
to be wearing a version of an Arendelle guard's

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.580
uniform, although it's worth noting that the
design is slightly off from the one we see

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.540
in Frozen.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:43.419
Either the royal guard uniform has been updated
in the past three years, or Matthias and his

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:48.980
men are wearing an older version of the uniform,
and have been in the forest for a long time.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:54.460
Perhaps the character we're most excited about,
though, is the tiny salamander named Bruni

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:58.200
whom we see excitedly lapping up Elsa's magic
snowflakes.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:03.700
Bruni was the most adorable part of the trailer,
and according to Olaf voice actor Josh Gad,

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:04.710
that's just the beginning.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:05.770
Gad tweeted:

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:08.120
"Meet your new future obsession.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.840
You have no idea."

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:15.200
So far in the Frozen-verse, whenever rocks
start shaking, it's nothing to worry about.

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:19.889
It's almost always the kindhearted, waist-high
trolls, the same gentle people who took in

00:07:19.889 --> 00:07:22.080
Kristoff when he was just a young boy.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.000
However, Frozen 2 looks to be introducing
a whole new breed of rock people in the form

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.140
of towering stone giants.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:32.500
And from the looks of things, they're not
very friendly.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:38.300
The trailer sees Anna and Olaf steering a
boat past a group of sleeping stone giants,

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.310
keeping quiet so as not to wake them.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:46.259
Later, we see Anna, Kristoff, and Sven fleeing
for their lives as a giant pursues them, hurling

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.900
rocks, and then a number of giants rising
up over the treetops.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:54.620
Although we're assuming that the stone giants
aren't the real villains here, they're certainly

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:59.200
a formidable opponent, and we're pretty excited
to see what sort of magic Elsa conjures against

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.200
them.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:06.620
It's a blink-and-you'll-miss-it shot, but
at one point in the trailer, Kristoff rides

00:08:06.639 --> 00:08:12.310
Sven into the forest and scoops up Anna, leaving
a person who appears to be Elsa behind on

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:13.540
her hands and knees.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:17.620
Apparently, Kristoff won't hesitate to save
Anna, even if it means leaving her sister

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:18.500
behind.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:24.200
It's not unexpected, especially if the rumors
from D23 are true and Kristoff plans to propose

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:27.800
to Anna in Frozen 2, but it does feel significant.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:32.560
We know from Frozen that Anna and Elsa will
always do everything they can to save one

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:37.540
another, but what happens if Kristoff decides
that saving Elsa is too risky for Anna?

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:42.060
We hope that Frozen 2 doesn't come down to
Anna having to choose between her boyfriend

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:45.690
and her sister, but if it does, there won't
be any contest.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.720
Sorry, Kris.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.200
Sisters before misters.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:52.800
In a film that is presumably all about learning
where its characters came from, it's fitting

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.260
that we could get a glimpse into the backstory
of one character you've probably never even

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.800
wondered about: Sven the reindeer.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:04.380
We know from Frozen that Sven has been with
Kristoff since he was a little boy, but we

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.280
never really learned where he was before that.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:12.560
Well, wonder no longer, as it looks like we
may finally get an answer to where Sven got

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:13.380
his start.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:19.320
In the Frozen 2 trailer, we see a young Northuldra
girl crossing a bridge cradling a baby reindeer.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:23.779
This looks a lot like the girl we saw earlier
in the trailer twirling in the air in the

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:28.200
enchanted forest, who may very well be Elsa
and Anna's mother, Iduna.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:33.360
It's very possible that either Sven or one
of his parents was born in the enchanted forest,

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:38.339
and came to Arendelle with Iduna and her people,
meaning that in Frozen 2, he'll be returning

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.640
to his natural home.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.320
This seems to be supported by shots in both
this and previous trailers of Sven running

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.220
happily with a herd of reindeer, possibly
his original family.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:52.980
While we have no doubt that he and Kristoff
will always remain brothers at heart, it could

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.800
be nice to see Sven finally find his place
among other reindeer.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.140
They are, after all, better than people.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:07.740
There are several shots in the new trailer
of characters rushing into battle, both Arendelle

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.160
soldiers and Northuldra warriors.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.580
At the beginning of the trailer, they seem
to be fighting each other, although it's hard

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:19.120
to be sure, while at the end, they're charging
toward some unseen foe.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:24.120
If they're fighting one another, it could
be the conflict Pabbie showed Elsa in her

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.000
vision, with the sword and the staff clashing
together.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:32.040
Alternately, the vision could be attempting
to mislead us, and might actually symbolize

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.960
the two groups coming together and fighting
as one.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:39.080
Either way, there's a strong chance that the
battle we keep glimpsing in the trailer isn't

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.080
actually one that takes place in the present
timeline.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.320
It's very possible that this fight is one
that took place long ago, and that's what

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.650
led to the barring of the enchanted forest.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:52.760
However, even if the conflict is an old one,
if it was between Arendelle, the Northuldra,

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:58.209
and the mysterious forces of the forest, all
of the elements are there for it to spin up

00:10:58.209 --> 00:10:59.840
again in Frozen 2.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:05.340
Perhaps this is why the Arendelle-born, magical
Elsa is so important, especially if it turns

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:11.010
out that her mother is Northuldra: she contains
elements of all three, and may be the one

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:14.120
who is finally able to bring about a lasting
peace.

